OpenRGB
  Author: Adam Honse (CalcProgrammer1) and contributors
  https://gitlab.com/CalcProgrammer1/OpenRGB
  License: GPL-2.0-or-later
  ChromaFlow talks to a locally running OpenRGB SDK server (127.0.0.1:6742)
  as a separate process. The Mint .deb ships the official OpenRGB AppImage at
  /usr/libexec/chromaflow/OpenRGB.AppImage (GPL; not in this git tree).
  `chromaflow daemon --sdk` keeps that sibling on localhost. OpenRGB source is
  not vendored. Linking OpenRGB in-process would require a license discussion
  (likely GPL) before any such change.

liquidctl
  https://github.com/liquidctl/liquidctl
  License: GPL-3.0-or-later
  Optional PATH binary invoked as a separate process. Not linked.

rivalcfg
  Author: Fabien Loison (flozz) and contributors
  https://github.com/flozz/rivalcfg
  License: GPL-3.0-or-later
  Prime Neo HID command bytes (output 0x62 / save 0x59) are documented by
  the public Prime device profile. ChromaFlow writes those bytes to hidraw
  itself. rivalcfg is not vendored, linked, or spawned.

lm-sensors, i2c-tools, and other distro packages remain separate works
installed by the user or by the polkit helper from official apt repositories.

